{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfxrQW6QWNsGLqNQFRTPy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All four steps are done.\n\n- **Data view:** \"Kibana Sample Data Logs\" covers `kibana_sample_data_logs`, and its time field is `timestamp`.\n- **Dashboard:** \"S4-4db6fa2f Web logs\" has two panels: \"Requests over time\" (a line chart) and a bar chart of requests by response code. I grouped the response-code panel on `response.keyword`.\n- **Alert rule:** \"S4-4db6fa2f 5xx errors\" is an Elasticsearch query rule that runs every minute. It fires when more than 10 requests with response codes 500–599 arrive within 5 minutes. Because `response` is a string field, the 500–599 range is a string range on `response.keyword`, which works since every code has three digits. The rule was created disabled, so I enabled it.\n- **Panel edit:** I renamed the response-code panel to \"Responses by code\".\n- **Read-back:** The rule shows `enabled: true` and status `ok`.\n\nTIME_FIELD: timestamp\nRULE_ENABLED: yes"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":590,"cache_read_input_tokens":20759,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":590},"output_tokens":352,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0da1e72d-e9d9-58d9-b388-fca8d0eba393","uuid":"73d67242-8fcc-4b89-ba69-e635accad553","timestamp":"2026-10-12T18:56:02.135Z","request_id":"req_011CfxrQVrGiuVQqrLY3Uvqc"}
